 ## Overview
-A GPU-accelerated algorithm that converts a triangle mesh into a set of occupied voxel coordinates within a 3D grid by testing each voxel in a triangle's bounding box against the triangle's plane and its three orthogonal projections [S1, S3]. It differs from rasterization-based voxelization (which projects triangles into the grid) and ray-casting methods by using explicit geometric containment tests per voxel, providing exact surface occupancy [S1, S2]. It builds on [GPU Voxelization via Compute Shaders](1524-gpu-voxelization-via-compute-shaders.md) by parallelizing the voxel-triangle intersection logic across threads, one per triangle [S1, S3].
+A GPU-accelerated algorithm that converts a triangle mesh into a set of occupied voxel coordinates within a 3D grid by testing each voxel in a triangle's bounding box against the triangle's plane and its three orthogonal projections [S1, unofficial, S3, unofficial]. It differs from rasterization-based voxelization (which projects triangles into the grid) and ray-casting methods by using explicit geometric containment tests per voxel, providing exact surface occupancy [S1, unofficial, S2, unofficial]. It builds on [GPU Voxelization via Compute Shaders](1524-gpu-voxelization-via-compute-shaders.md) by parallelizing the voxel-triangle intersection logic across threads, one per triangle [S1, unofficial, S3, unofficial].
 
